{
  "metric": "Transactions in the latest observed block",
  "pollIntervalSeconds": 30,
  "definition": "Length of the transaction-hash array returned by each network public RPC for its latest accepted/mined block. System/protocol transactions are included if the RPC lists them. No unique-user, value, TPS, daily-total, or complete-stream claim is made.",
  "interpretation": [
    "This is a periodic sample, not every block or every transaction. Blocks on different networks cover different durations and are observed at slightly different times.",
    "Latest EVM blocks are not checked for finality and can reorganize. Starknet acceptance level is returned explicitly.",
    "A successful RPC fetch does not guarantee the provider is at the network tip. Block age and source-check age both gate the live display.",
    "Failures return per-chain unavailable with null metrics. No saved observation is used as a live fallback.",
    "Public endpoints can impose rate limits or availability restrictions. Cartridge answered unauthenticated server probes; its docs describe API-token or domain access requirements, so future refusal remains unavailable rather than bypassed."
  ],
